The model weights are downloaded at run time from the Hugging Face Hub; this package pins one revision of
each of these repositories (jev_style/models.py) and includes none of them:

* chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-0.8B-Decision-v3 and its -MLX / -GGUF builds: a fine-tuned derivative of
  Qwen3.5-0.8B (Copyright 2026 Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0).
* chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-2B-Decision-v3 and its -MLX / -GGUF builds: a fine-tuned derivative of
  Qwen3.5-2B (Copyright 2026 Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0).
* chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-2B-Decision-v4 and its -MLX / -GGUF builds: a fine-tuned derivative of
  Qwen3.5-2B (Copyright 2026 Alibaba Cloud, Apache-2.0), trained in part on soft labels distilled from
  TypeSafe Jev 1.14 through its public API, as its model card discloses.

See the NOTICE file of each model repository for the modifications and training sources of that release.

The question types (choice / score / noul) and the request shape follow the public typed-decision
("systemone") convention so the same client code works against different servers.

Not affiliated with, endorsed by or connected to TypeSafe or Jev. "Jev-Style" only describes the kind
of model (a small typed-decision model in a similar style); no Jev weights or code are included, and this
package distributes no raw teacher API responses. Not affiliated with or endorsed by Alibaba Cloud / the Qwen
team, the Laya authors, the Kev authors or the JevK5 author.

The named cascade cascade-9b and jevk5: cascade tiers use JevK5-9B by alibiserikbay
(alibiserikbay/JevK5-9B, Apache-2.0) through its runtime jevk5 (github.com/allebee/jevk5, Apache-2.0).
Neither is included: the runtime is installed separately and the weights are downloaded at run time from
their own repository. Per its model card, part of JevK5-9B's training labels were generated by OpenAI's
GPT-6 Luna and are subject to OpenAI's terms. tests/conftest.py mirrors jevk5's question validation
(jevk5/server.py, v0.3.3, Apache-2.0) for its fake jevk5 module.

Web demos: see the LICENSES.md file inside each folder under jev_style/web/ for third-party data.
